<sub>2</sub>) less than 8.0&#x02009;kPa (60&#x02009;mm&#x02009;Hg) with or without arterial partial pressure of CO<sub>2</sub> (PaCO<sub>2</sub>) greater than 6.7&#x02009;kPa (50&#x02009;mm&#x02009;Hg) while breathing air at sea level. </p></fn><fn><p>Adapted from <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.goldcopd.com/">http://www.goldcopd.com/</ext-link>, updated 2009.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>